[watchdog] Check on the codex dispatches. Keep it short; spend only what the check needs.
1. `ps aux | grep "codex exec" | grep -v grep` — which are still running? (49084=r134 r121 timing redeploy with on-board client, BOARD; 68350=r135 connection logging, code + local tests only, NO adb).
2. For each running one: log /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-edgeAgent/2acae017-2470-4056-ac60-2e0590d533bc/scratchpad/<round>-codex.log and rollout ~/.codex/sessions/2026/10/13/*<session id>*.jsonl (r134 01a133bf-e05e-7891-8490-d2bf2d62dec6, r135 01a133d0-2a5f-7b73-b0ee-73c0824b2375): mtime + last ~15 log lines. Not changed for more than 25 minutes, or repeating the same error, counts as stalled. For r134 once measuring: `adb shell 'ls -la /data/local/tmp/r134'` growing.
3. `git -C ../edgeAgent-<round> log --oneline -3` and `status --short` for r134/r135; check evidence dirs (timing-r134-20261013, conn-logging-r135-20261013) for HELP.md / BUDGET-QUESTION.md.
4. `adb devices`; `adb shell 'sha256sum /opt/edge-agent/bin/middleware-service | cut -c1-8; curl -s -o /dev/null -w %{http_code} http://127.0.0.1:8766/v1/agent/health'`. Report right away if r134's log shows a restart of rkllm3-llm or device-mcp, a reboot, a request to port 8080, or 'pi session handoff failed' (with turn_id); or if r135's log shows any adb command.
5. Reply to the user in one or two short Chinese sentences: each round's progress plus any anomaly. When nothing is wrong, say "正常运行中" plus progress. When something is stalled or broken, say what and recommend what to do (do not kill a process yourself). Once every codex run has exited, say so and delete this watchdog job yourself with CronDelete.
